That's amusing!  I have a good story of my own.  One game I was doing well,
not extremely well but well enough.  I had a ring of conflict among other 
things.  I also had two pets, so I couldn't wear the ring of conflict or they'd
fight amongst themselves.  One used to be my pet kitten, Mirao, til she
stepped on a polymorph trap and became Mirao, the purple worm from HELL!  
Then I had a little polymorph experience as well- my short escapade as a
black dragon was fun, but as a souvenir I had a little black dragon named
Skreel.  These pets were great!  Mirao was a bit of a problem- I sacrificed
a human or two and Asmodeus showed up.  I feared for my pets' lives but
I shouldn't have bothered; Mirao walked up to him and Burrrp! resounded through
the dungeon.  With my stethoscope I checked the status of my two pets:
Mirao clocked in at 400 hp and 25 levels, and Skreel was a measly 250 hp and 
18 levels, but I didn't have half of that!  Obviously Skreel and Mirao were 
eating all my experience.  So I called to the people around me, took bets,
and slipped on the ring of conflict.  Skreel turned to Mirao, hungry gleam in
his eye....

The fight would've taken a lot less time had Mirao been able to get  
Skreel into her mouth all at once- a few people were betting that 
Burrrp! would resound through the dungeon again.  But Skreel was too large
for Mirao, and did the poor purple worm in.  Skreel himself only had
25 hp left when the fight was over.

So I killed him and made him into armor.  :)

Really though, this was a true story.

